1183		\uses{lem:qld-4-10, fact:data-processing}
1184		Define
1185		$\hat{Q}^{x,z,\alpha,\beta}_{c}
1186		= \sum_{a,b \,:\, \alpha a + \beta b = c} \hat{Q}^{x,z}_{a,b}$,
1187		a coarse-graining of the projective measurement of
1188		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10}, hence itself projective. A uniformly random
1189		point of $\F_q^{2m+2}$ has uniformly random coordinates $(x,z)$, so the
1190		self-consistency and consistency properties follow from those of
1191		$\{\hat{Q}^{x,z}_{a,b}\}$ established in Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10}
1192		together with Lemma~\ref{fact:data-processing}, which shows that
